                <pb facs="0356" n="346" sameAs="frus:frus1948v08/pg346"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.3393/12–2747: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Tsingtao</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Spiker</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tsingtao</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1947-12-27T14:00:00+08:00">December 27, 1947—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 27—6:01 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>138. Four Marine enlisted men on hunting excursion in jeep were seized by
                    Communists noon, December 25 at 2 kilometers northwest Lingshan, 36 miles north
                    of Tsingtao. Party was 18 miles north of authorized hunting limits. Arms
                    included 3 shot guns, 1 carbine. Jeep destroyed by burning. No word has been
                    received from or concerning missing men.</p>
                <p>Sent Embassy 1645; repeated Department 138.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Spiker</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
